{
  "case_id": "2020-20-157",
  "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Shay Dvoretzky",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Fourth Amendment recognizes the sanctity of the home by drawing a firm line at the door. The government cannot cross that line without a warrant, unless there is consent or exigent circumstances."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dvoretzky",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DVORETZKY: Justice Sotomayor, I don't mean to fight too hard on the hypothetical that the Chief Justice presented. The emergency aid doctrine, if -- if that could cover that sort of situation, it -- it would also cover lots of other situations that the other side is positing today require a community caretaking exception. The -- the emergency aid doctrine can -- covers true emergencies if there is reasonable cause to believe that someone is in need."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dvoretzky",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That doesn't help the Respondents in this case. They haven't argued exigent circumstances. In fact, they've affirmatively waived exigent circumstances."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Justice KAGAN."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: And under what standard do those laws operate? Is it a probable cause standard? Is it something lower? Could it be something lower?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dvoretzky",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "With an admin -- Justice Gorsuch, with an administrative warrant requirement, you're involving a neutral decisionmaker rather than leaving it --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "day on average, every single day on average, there are 65 suicides by gunshot in the United States on average every day, okay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Petitioner has an absolute position: Under no circumstances should a warrantless caretaking occur inside a home, except upon consent or exigent circumstances. This absolute all-or-nothing approach is contrary to the reasonableness standard of the Fourth Amendment, the very touchstone of the Fourth Amendment. There may be circumstances that allow for caretaking in the home absent a warrant, when the advent of the potential harm is not so clear but the need to respond could be immediate. Time could be of the essence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In this case, the absolute position taken by the Petitioner, not allowing the caretaking actions, may have resulted in death or injury, and that's why an absolute prohibition against warrantless entry is wrong. Community caretaking in the home without a warrant should be allowed when it is objectively reasonable to do so."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: My question --my problem is that if you take a caretaker exception and read that into the word \"reasonable,\" there's no stopping. We don't know how far we'll go. But, if you are absolute, you may cause a different problem. So we're looking for subsidiary standards. Camara says you need a warrant for administrative searches, but it uses words like \"normally\" and so forth, so there's some wiggle room there."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, let me just interrupt because I have very little time. What about the amount of information that the -- the government officer has to have? Probable cause? Reasonable suspicion? Something else?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0003-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "you said, well, the Fourth Amendment has only one test, but I kind of think, if there's any one principle of the Fourth Amendment law that this Court has created, it's that the home is special and that the automobile is distinctly not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Ratner",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0003-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case is fundamentally different from most of the Court's Fourth Amendment cases because the question is not act now or get a warrant first. It's act now or not at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Ratner",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0003-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think the community caretaking label is a little misleading because, again, Cady was so bound up in the particular circumstances of vehicles and that the better rule here is that there be specific facts that objectively establish a non-investigatory justification, in particular, the need for assistance, and that the scope of the official's actions be reasonably tailored to that interest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Right. I'm just asking. I mean, what do you think?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. RATNER: If we had to decide right now, I would say probably not, that we're --we think that the risk of harm to a person is --is really the core that could match the --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Good morning, Ms. Ratner. Let me see if I understand what -- what you said this morning because it differs a little bit from my reading of your brief. You -- you agree we should look to the common law to inform our understanding of the Fourth Amendment's reasonableness test?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0004-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our argument we've -- we've defended today is that the serious government interest, the government interest that's been called paramount, an individual's safety, is one that can match the significant privacy interests in the home. We don't think the Court should get into harms to property or abatement of nuisances here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0005-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 106,
        "start": 106
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why can't you see the difference? Why Can't your rule articulate that difference in a more reasonable way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0005-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 107,
        "start": 107
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He answered the door. He did not want to be helped."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-157",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0005-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 109,
        "start": 109
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
